  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REDUCING DEMAND FOR PANGOLINS THROUGH COMMUNITY-BASED SOCIAL MARKETING</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO COUNTER WILDLIFE TRAFFICKING FROM PANGOLIN RANGE STATES IN AFRICA AND ASIA TO CHINA, BY LAYING THE FOUNDATIONS FOR REDUCING CONSUMER DEMAND FOR PANGOLIN IN THREE CHINESE PROVINCES IDENTIFIED AS BEING MAJOR HUBS FOR CONSUMPTION OF ILLEGALLY TRADED WILDLIFE. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE ALL EIGHT SPECIES OF PANGOLIN BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACT OF CONSUMER DEMAND IN CHINA WHICH DRIVES POACHING AND TRAFFICKING IN PANGOLIN RANGE STATES. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE 1 SELECTING PRECISE BEHAVIOURS TO CHANGE 2 IDENTIFYING BARRIERS AND BENEFITS TO DESIRED BEHAVIOURS 3 DEVELOPING STRATEGIES TO CHANGE BEHAVIOURS 4 PILOTING THE BEHAVIOUR CHANGE STRATEGIES AND 5 BROAD-SCALE IMPLEMENTATION.THE SCOPE OF WORK WAS CHANGED TO SHIFT PROPOSED ACTIVITIES FROM CHINA TO THAILAND IN SPRING 2020. THE SHIFT TO THAILAND WAS IN RESPONSE TO THE RECIPIENT BEING UNABLE TO REGISTER TO LEGALLY OPERATE IN CHINA DUE TO NEW LAWS THAT WERE PUT IN PLACE AFTER THE GRANT WASAWARDED. THE RECIPIENT WILL CARRY OUT THE ORIGINAL ACTIVITIES IN THAILAND WITH A CONTINUED FOCUS ON THE SAME TARGET POPULATION CONSUMERS OF PANGOLIN PRODUCTS . CARRYING OUT THIS WORK IN THAILAND IS PART OF THE RECIPIENT S EXISTING PROGRAM STRATEGY IN THAILAND AND THE RECIPIENT IS ALREADY CARRYING OUT SIMILAR, ONGOING ACTIVITIES.</narrative>
  </description>
